  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 354 AM CDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nHigh pressure settles over the region today with sunny skies & \nseasonable temperatures in the low to mid 60s. Clear skies and \nlight winds tonight will create ideal radiational cooling\nconditions, with temperatures falling into the mid to upper 30s\nacross central Minnesota & western Wisconsin and generally low \n40s elsewhere. Issued a Frost Advisory for portions of central\nMinnesota & western Wisconsin, with areas of frost most likely \nin rural & low-lying areas through sunrise. Take care to protect\nany sensitive vegetation in these areas\n\nUpper level ridging builds over the central CONUS through the \nweek, leading to a stretch of dry weather along with generally \nabove normal temperatures. Highs most days will end up in the \nmid to upper 60s, with the exception of Tuesday when stronger \nsoutherly flow ahead of a frontal passage raises temperatures \nwell into the 70s. Temperatures warm back into the mid 60s \nMonday before southerly flow pushes highs well into the 70s \nTuesday. Little chance for precipitation through the week, with \nthe next shot at rain looking possible for the latter half of \nnext weekend",
